LinTranslator — third-party notices and model licences
===============================================

LinTranslator itself has no licence file yet. Choose one (MIT / Apache-2.0 / GPL-3.0)
before publishing; this file covers everything LinTranslator uses, downloads or is
built around.

The short version, because it is the one that can bite a user:

  The default local translation model, facebook/nllb-200-distilled-600M, is
  licensed CC-BY-NC-4.0 — NON-COMMERCIAL USE ONLY.

  LinTranslator does not bundle or redistribute those weights. `lintranslator convert`
  downloads them from HuggingFace onto the user's own machine, and the local
  backends load them from there. So the licence binds whoever runs the local
  backend, not whoever distributes LinTranslator's source.

  It does bind a distributor who ships pre-converted weights, and it binds
  anyone using the local backend for paid or commercial work.


Downloaded at runtime
---------------------

facebook/nllb-200-distilled-600M  (and any other NLLB checkpoint)
    Licence: CC-BY-NC-4.0
    https://huggingface.co/facebook/nllb-200-distilled-600M
    Used by the `ct2` (default) and `local` backends. Non-commercial only.
    This includes derived artefacts: the int8 directory `lintranslator convert`
    produces is a derivative of the weights and carries the same terms, so
